from fast_reference_helpers import *
P='src-b88-'
rows=[
 ('miracleman','List of Miracleman story arcs','Wikipedia contributors','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Miracleman_story_arcs','secondary_plot_reference','Olympus-era rulers abolish money, make goods free, restore fertility and provide plentiful sustainable energy; the Golden Age retains selective refusals of help.','Technological Qys/Warpsmith interventions are part of the mechanism; not every miracle or every personal request is guaranteed.'),
 ('authority','Meet the Authority','DC editorial staff','https://www.dc.com/blog/2021/07/20/meet-the-authority-the-anti-justice-league','publisher_overview','The Engineer has nanomachines and the team uses the Carrier.','Powers and a headquarters do not establish implemented global ordinary provision.'),
 ('redson','Superman: Red Son','Wikipedia contributors','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Superman:_Red_Son','secondary_plot_reference','Brainiac becomes Superman’s aide, poverty/unemployment disappear, and dissidents become surgically controlled human drones.','No unemployment is not nonworking; human-derived drones are not erased as mere production machinery.'),
 ('allstar','All-Star Superman 10 review','Neal Bailey, Superman Homepage','https://www.supermanhomepage.com/comics/2008-post-crisis-reviews/c-review-2008.php?topic=allstarsup10','secondary_issue_review','Kandorians take steps to aid Superman and discuss relocation.','A miniature city’s rescue is not a material allocation charter.'),
 ('krypton','Krypton (comics)','Wikipedia contributors','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Krypton_(comics)','secondary_continuity_reference','Different Kryptons use robots, career allocation and technological citadels.','Continuities differ; no single machine economy or universal floor can be assigned to every depiction.'),
 ('kandor','Kandor (comics)','Wikipedia contributors','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kandor_(comics)','secondary_continuity_reference','Different versions feature confinement, rescue, artificial support and relocation.','Care under a captor and a city’s miniature scale do not by themselves establish work-independent ordinary allocation.'),
 ('legion','Legion of Super-Heroes 1989 issue 1 index','Grand Comics Database contributors','https://www.comics.org/issue/46932/','bibliographic_issue_index','The issue includes a text feature about the U.P. tech-economy collapse.','An index and headline are not a full economy passage; no complete Legion run read.'),
 ('million','DC One Million','Wikipedia contributors','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DC_One_Million','secondary_plot_reference','Far-future heroes, artificial entities and Solaris define the crossover.','Advanced beings and solar engineering do not establish ordinary residents’ access or work participation.'),
 ('maker','Transmetropolitan Maker passage reproduced in University of Alberta thesis','University of Alberta thesis text; byline not checked','https://www.collectionscanada.gc.ca/obj/thesescanada/vol2/AEU/TC-AEU-1037.pdf','indexed_primary_quote_in_secondary_analysis','Issue 2’s column explains household makers, costly feedstock, garbage converters and exclusion of households without makers.','Only the bounded indexed Maker passage and nearby issue 19 discussion; no PDF download or whole thesis read.'),
 ('transmet-review','Signal and noise: world building in Transmetropolitan','Comics Bookcase contributor','https://www.comicsbookcase.com/features-archive/2020/2/27/comics-anatomy-signal-and-noise-an-exploration-of-world-building-in-transmetropolitan','secondary_criticism','Revivals illustrate continued technological neglect and poverty.','Critical description, not an estimate of all-person employment.'),
 ('tokyo','Tokyo Ghost collected-volume description','Rick Remender/Image Comics, Google Play Books listing','https://play.google.com/store/books/series?id=4sjXFwAAABA03M','publisher_description','Technology addiction and gangster rule shape Los Angeles; constables perform enforcement work.','Entertainment dependence does not establish automatic material provision.'),
 ('lazarus','Lazarus (comics)','Wikipedia contributors','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lazarus_(comics)','secondary_setting_reference','Families dominate genetic technology, serfs have useful occupations, and Waste can be lifted into skilled work.','Class exclusion and modified crops do not establish a demonstrated automated productive floor.'),
 ('lazarus-criticism','Lazarus as a frightening future vision','Salon contributor','https://www.salon.com/2017/01/06/the-comic-book-lazarus-is-a-frightening-vision-of-where-america-could-be-headed/','secondary_criticism','Family medical advantages coexist with serf/Waste exclusion, including Hock oppression.','Life extension and deprivation do not independently establish post-work technological replacement.')
]
S=cited_sources(P,rows)
refs=[P+'miracleman']
R=[scoped_record('c0749','miracleman-olympus-earth','Miracleman — Olympus-era Earth','Miracleman','The established free-provision order under Miracleman and his allies',['comic'],
 'Olympus and Golden Age comic story arcs','The implemented utopian order after the London catastrophe','Living human residents of the transformed Earth',
 ['Every requested cure as automatically granted','Resurrected artificial bodies as a measured additional human population','An ordinary democratic mandate inferred from public approval'],
 'Miracleman and his allies replace the old economy with a technologically transformed Earth where money is abolished and goods are free. Warpsmith and Qys capabilities help reshape material conditions, while abundant sustainable energy and restored fertile land support ordinary life. The guarantee estimate is strong for that implemented order. It is qualified by the rulers’ discretion: the later Golden Age includes a refusal to help a father’s brain-damaged daughter, so universal fulfillment of every personal need would overstate the evidence.\n\nControl remains concentrated in the superhuman leadership and its alien collaborators. This is a disclosed analogy to the concentrated non-AI position, not a claim that alien or enhanced biological rulers are machines. Popular approval does not establish equal ownership or a right to overrule Olympus. Useful art, care, research and public services can continue even without money. The story summary supplies no all-person work census, so nonworking remains unresolved rather than treating universal free goods as universal idleness.',
 [-.75,0,None],[[-1,-.15],[0,.15],None],['The implemented Olympus order explicitly abolishes money, supplies free goods and transforms productive energy/ecology through advanced allied technology.','Superhuman and alien biological rulers concentrate authority; 0 is an explicit non-AI elite analogy.','Free goods and abolished currency do not census useful chosen labor.'],refs,1)]
refs=[P+'maker',P+'transmet-review']
R.append(scoped_record('c0757','transmetropolitan-maker-city','Transmetropolitan — The City’s unequal Maker economy','Transmetropolitan','Household fabrication amid continued class exclusion',['comic'],
 'Original comic, issue 2 Maker column and related City depictions','Established City life during Spider Jerusalem’s reporting','Living humans and human-derived City residents',
 ['Every citizen as owning a Maker','Body modification as automatic provision','People revived into neglect as guaranteed secure housing'],
 'Makers can fabricate meals, clothing and other goods within an ordinary household. The comic’s own column explains that middle-class families can afford a machine while its ideal feedstock is far more expensive; garbage converters offer a less efficient substitute. Families without Makers continue buying packaged necessities, and competition for reusable refuse exposes the class divide. This is actual automatic material production with uneven access, rather than a purely theoretical invention.\n\nGuarantees are weak because neither the machine nor its inputs are universally supplied, and the broader City continues to neglect vulnerable residents. Household possession disperses some productive capacity, but ownership of the relevant infrastructure and inputs is not established as equally shared; control remains unresolved instead of reading private appliances as a democratic commons. Human-derived residents remain visible despite changes of body. Journalism, fabrication design, cleaning, care and other useful work continue, while deprivation is not a nonworking statistic. The point describes the unequal implemented economy and does not duplicate it as a separate zero variant solely because access is restricted.',
 [.8,None,None],[[.4,1],None,None],['Issue 2 explicitly describes actual household material fabrication and costly inputs; people without machines remain dependent on purchases.','Personal Maker ownership is widespread in one class, but effective control of productive infrastructure and input supplies remains unresolved.','Neither Maker ownership nor poverty supplies an all-person useful-work census.'],refs,3,proxy=True))

cases=[
 ('c0750','authority','The short Authority overview establishes transformative powers, not implemented global work-independent provision.','The Carrier and Engineer’s object creation cannot substitute for ordinary population access rules.'),
 ('c0751','redson','Eliminated poverty and unemployment do not establish how automation separates necessities from labor.','Brainiac administration and surgically controlled human workers coexist; no human leisure or job-preservation mechanism is inferred.'),
 ('c0752','allstar','All-Star Kandor’s rescue and relocation do not establish its ordinary productive/access system.','Miniaturization and hero assistance leave material distribution unresolved.'),
 ('c0753','krypton','Krypton’s heterogeneous advanced civilizations lack a verified common allocation system.','Robot assistance, assigned careers and isolated citadels must not be merged across continuities into one welfare score.'),
 ('c0754','kandor','Bottle-city support does not establish a distinct ordinary post-work allocation order.','Different captors and continuities require concrete provision details; no unsupported duplication of All-Star is retained.'),
 ('c0755','legion','The United Planets’ advanced technology and an economy-collapse headline do not establish a common material floor.','A specific period and accessible household rules are missing; the issue index is not treated as a read story.'),
 ('c0756','million','853rd-century beings and solar engineering do not establish ordinary material access.','A giant time gap and advanced artificial heroes are not labor or ownership evidence.'),
 ('c0758','tokyo','Los Angeles technology addiction does not establish automatic ordinary necessities.','Gangster power and useful constable work leave the productive/distribution mechanism unverified.'),
 ('c0759','lazarus','Lazarus class exclusion and genetic crop control lack a verified automation-to-allocation link.','Waste is a political class, not an automatic census of people made redundant by machines.'),
 ('c0760','lazarus-criticism','Hock oppression does not independently establish a distinct post-work technological economy.','Medical dependency and serf exploitation are insufficient without the productive mechanism; no whole sourcebook rescue.')
]
D=[short_disposition(cid,'needs_evidence',why,[P+key],analysis) for cid,key,why,analysis in cases]
D += [decision(r['candidate_id'],'included','The bounded reference establishes actual technological material provision with explicit access limits.',r['source_ids'],society_id=r['id']) for r in R]
D.sort(key=lambda x:x['candidate_id'])
write_batch(88,[f'c{i:04}' for i in range(749,761)],S,R,D,[
 'Twelve sequential short-reference dispositions, two retained records. Unclear superhero economies were not rescued by reading long continuity histories.',
 'Miracleman’s alien/superhuman rulers use an explicit concentrated non-AI analogy; discretionary medical refusal qualifies guarantees.',
 'Transmetropolitan is supported by a bounded indexed primary Maker column reproduced in analysis, not merely by fan speculation about replicators. No PDF retrieval or render.',
 'Red Son’s no-unemployment statement is not converted to nonworking; surgically altered humans remain human-derived workers.',
 'Unrelated musical-authority, Krypton engineering-company and academic nanotechnology results were discarded.'
])
